---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site, mailto } from '../site';

// The full refund and cancellation policy. Section 6 of the terms summarises
// it and links here; keep the two in step. The numbers come from site.ts.
const { windowDays, issuedWithin } = site.refunds;
const { responseTime } = site.support;
---

<Legal
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Refund policy',
    description: 'How buying a course works on PadiLearn, when you can get a refund, and how to ask for one.',
  }}
>
  <p>
    This policy covers courses bought on PadiLearn, in the web app at app.padilearn.com and in the Android app
    downloaded from padilearn.com. PadiLearn is operated by {site.company.name}. This policy is part of our
    <a href="/terms">terms of service</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>In short:</strong> if you were charged and didn't get your course, were charged twice, or the course
      is clearly not what it said, email <a href={mailto('Refund request')}>{site.supportEmail}</a> with your
      payment reference. For a course that isn't as described, ask within {windowDays} days of buying. We reply
      {responseTime}.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What you are buying</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Access to a video course</strong>, for your own learning, for as long as your account is open and
      the course stays on PadiLearn. It is a one-off payment in naira, not a subscription.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Courses are digital.</strong> Nothing is shipped, so there is nothing to return. Where a refund is
      due, we refund the payment instead.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>You see the full price before you pay:</strong> the course price set by its teacher, plus a card
      processing fee that covers what our payment provider charges. The total shown is the total charged.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Try before you buy.</strong> Many courses have a free preview lesson, and every course lists its
      lessons before you buy.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Delivery</h2>
  <p>
    Payment is handled by <strong>Paystack</strong>. The course appears in your account as soon as Paystack
    confirms the payment, usually within seconds. If it hasn't appeared after 10 minutes, don't pay again: email
    us with your payment reference (it is in the receipt Paystack emails you) and we'll sort it out.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancellations</h2>
  <p>
    There are no subscriptions or automatic renewals, so there is nothing to cancel after you buy. If you leave
    the checkout before paying, you are not charged.
  </p>

  <h2>When you can get a refund</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>What happened</th><th>What we do</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>You were charged but the course never appeared</td>
        <td>We give you the course. If we can't, we refund what you paid.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>You were charged more than once for the same course</td>
        <td>We refund every extra payment in full. You keep the course.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>We removed the course because it broke our terms</td>
        <td>Everyone who paid for it gets a full refund, card fee included. We contact you; you don't need to ask.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>The course is clearly not what its description and preview showed</td>
        <td>
          Ask within {windowDays} days of buying. We review the request, and if it is upheld we refund what you paid.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>The course won't play because of a fault on our side that we can't fix</td>
        <td>We refund what you paid.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    We don't refund a change of mind, a course you have mostly watched, or a request made more than {windowDays} days
    after buying, except in the cases above or where the law says otherwise. Free courses cost nothing, so there is
    nothing to refund.
  </p>

  <h2>How to ask for a refund</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Email <a href={mailto('Refund request')}>{site.supportEmail}</a> from the address on your PadiLearn account,
      with the subject "Refund request".
    </li>
    <li>Include the course title, your payment reference, and what went wrong.</li>
    <li>We reply {responseTime}, and tell you whether the refund is approved and why.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>After a refund is approved</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We send it through Paystack {issuedWithin}, back to the card or bank account you paid with.</li>
    <li>Your bank may take up to 10 working days to show it. That part is outside our control.</li>
    <li>
      A refunded course is removed from your account, except when you were charged twice: then only the extra
      payment is refunded, and the course stays yours.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Card disputes</h2>
  <p>
    Please contact us before disputing a payment with your bank: we can usually fix things faster. If a dispute is
    decided in your favour, the course is removed from your account.
  </p>

  <h2>Teachers</h2>
  <p>
    When a sale is refunded, the teacher's share of it is taken back. Paystack usually pays teachers the next working
    day, so by the time a refund is approved the teacher has often been paid: the same amount is then kept back from
    their next sales. The student's refund never waits for that. See
    <a href="/terms#teacher-earnings-and-payouts">teacher earnings and payouts</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing in this policy takes away your rights under the Federal Competition and Consumer Protection Act 2018 or
    any other Nigerian law. If we can't resolve a complaint with you, you can contact the Federal Competition and
    Consumer Protection Commission (FCCPC).
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {site.company.name}, operator of PadiLearn ·
    <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a> · <a href="/support">Support</a>
  </p>
</Legal>
